! How `reference.stm.al-metal` was made: `pw.x < al-metal.in` (with an outdir
! and prefix added), then `pp.x < al-metal.pp.in`. `plot_num = 5` is
! `PP/src/stm.f90` and `sample_bias = 0` collapses its window onto the Fermi
! level, which is Elk's task 162 -- so QE's image is defumat's delta-weighted
! one times `degauss`. The comparison is in
! `tests/regression/test_stm.py::test_the_tunnelling_density_matches_pp_x`.
!
! `filplot` is what the test reads: `Modules/plot_io.f90` writes the whole dense
! FFT grid as text, so nothing is interpolated on either side.
 &inputpp
    prefix='al'
    outdir='./out'
    filplot='al.stm'
    plot_num=5
    sample_bias=0.0
 /
 &plot
    nfile=1
    filepp(1)='al.stm'
    weight(1)=1.0
    iflag=3
    output_format=6
    fileout='al.stm.cube'
 /
